<%#
  What the guest sees the moment they press Send.

  The whole chat region is replaced rather than the message appended, because
  the first message is the case that has to work: until it exists the page has
  no thread, and therefore no stream subscription -- so the reply has to hand
  over the subscription, the log and the box as one piece. The bot's answer
  arrives later down that subscription, from the job.

  The replacement also empties the box and drops the "ask us anything" prompt,
  neither of which needs saying separately.
%>
<%= turbo_stream.replace PublicUI::Chat::Panel::REGION_ID do %>
  <%= render "public/concierge/chats/conversation",
        conversation: @conversation, messages: @messages, hotel: @hotel %>
<% end %>

<%# Always replaced, never only added: the region has to be able to clear the
    last refusal as well as show a new one. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "concierge-chat-error" do %>
  <div id="concierge-chat-error">
    <%= render "public/concierge/shared/error_alert", message: @error %>
  </div>
<% end %>
